"program_narrative": "INQPORT is an online (CICS) portfolio position inquiry program. It copies the caller's communication area (INQCOM layout) into working storage, registers CICS ERROR and NOTFND handlers, and reads the position record from the VSAM file POSFILE using the account number from the commarea as the key. When the read returns NORMAL the position is shown on the POSMAP screen (mapset INQSET); otherwise the message 'Position not found for account' is placed in the commarea and returned to the caller. The ERROR handler P999-ERROR-ROUTINE, reachable only at run time, returns 'Error accessing position data' and the CICS response code in the commarea. Several data names used by the logic (WS-COMMAREA-ACCOUNT-NO, POSITION-ACCOUNT, and the INQCOM fields qualified by WS-COMMAREA) do not resolve to declared fields and need SME review. The program ends with EXEC CICS RETURN.",
